      en: {
        productName: "Meta Muse personal AI agent",
        productType: "Muse is Meta's consumer personal AI agent, reached through the Muse app, WhatsApp, and muse.ai rather than being only a question-answering model. Meta built a Muse Secure VM: a dedicated cloud computer that houses the agent, personal data, and credentials for connected services. A separate Sentinel agent runs on the same machine but is isolated at the system level. Meta puts persistent memory, proactive suggestions, web services, email, and payment actions in one product story and says Muse will later reach AI glasses.",
        interactionFlow: "A user tells Muse a goal in chat: send an email, book travel, turn an Instagram-saved recipe into a grocery list, or keep moving a personal project forward. Muse can remember a preference mentioned once, call selected apps, and ask permission before sensitive actions such as sending or purchasing. Sentinel checks whether Muse may reach the internet. Meta says passwords and payment methods live in secure storage, so Muse cannot see the raw credentials. The user can give an app read-only mail access or permission to send on their behalf, disconnect it, ask Muse to forget a specific memory, and inspect a complete audit trail of what Muse has done and plans to do.",
        specsOrStack: "The disclosed system includes the Muse app, WhatsApp, muse.ai, the Muse Spark model, Muse Secure VM, a separate Sentinel agent, secure credential storage, connected third-party services, and an audit trail. Muse runs on a dedicated cloud computer. Meta says it will introduce Confidential VM later this year, encrypting the entire VM, data, and conversations with a key held only by the user. The announcement does not state the cloud provider, regional placement, hardware, model parameters, context limit, network-isolation implementation, audit-log format, connection limit, end-to-end latency, or enterprise-management API; these remain source not stated.",
        useCases: "Meta's examples include sending email, booking travel, checking out a purchase, turning a saved video recipe into a grocery list, and planning a dinner while remembering guests' dietary restrictions. Link built by Stripe lets Muse check out on eligible purchases and adds protections for damaged or lost items, price drops, no-fee returns, and return guarantees under its terms. Personal memory is aimed at repeated work involving preferences, calendars, friends, and longer goals. AI-glasses integration is described as coming soon, not as a generally available hardware capability today.",
        painPointsSolved: "Muse addresses the problem that personal tasks need sustained context, multiple apps, and sensitive credentials. A conventional chat can suggest an action but not safely carry it through; a conventional automation can execute but lacks a natural-language entry and personal memory. Secure VM attempts to join the two while app-level access choices define the agent's boundary. It does not automatically solve model misunderstanding, wrong purchases, mistaken emails, third-party service changes, audit overload, or proactive interruption. A security architecture can reduce exposure without making every task safe to run without a human check.",
        userVoice: "There is not enough independent long-duration user testing in this issue to verify Muse's task-success rate, memory accuracy, proactive-suggestion frequency, or payment-failure recovery. The official announcement provides architecture, permission, and security claims rather than an independent security audit or user-experience dataset. Claims that the product cannot fail, is completely private, or works across every service would exceed the available evidence.",
        newTech: "Muse's technology signal is the productisation of the agent runtime itself. Secure VM puts the agent and personal data in a dedicated environment; Sentinel separates internet approval from the main agent; secure storage lets the agent use credentials without seeing passwords; Confidential VM would move the trust root further toward a key held by the user. The combination makes security boundary, memory, permissions, and proactive action part of the HCI instead of leaving them to a settings page.",
        availability: "Meta says Muse is rolling out in the United States on iOS, Android, and muse.ai. It is free for most needs, with subscriptions for people who want more. AI-glasses support is coming soon. The announcement does not give full subscription prices, free limits, regional expansion dates, supported-service list, enterprise edition, or an exact Confidential VM launch date. Link purchase protection applies only to eligible transactions under Link and Stripe terms.",
        limitsOrUnknowns: "Open questions include which apps Muse can connect to, the finest permission granularity for each app, how Sentinel handles false approvals and refusals, whether audit trails can be exported, default memory retention, deletion from backups, the model/VM training boundary, cross-device login, minors, payment recovery, regional regulation, and Confidential VM key recovery. Real usage is needed to tell whether proactive memory and suggestions feel helpful or become another notification burden.",
        productVerdict: "Muse is a released personal-agent product whose most important deliverable is the Secure VM plus visible access and audit layers, not Muse Spark alone. It gives a long-lived agent a clearer product boundary: connect services, store credentials, retain memory, and ask before sensitive action. Verdict: confirmed product; observe task success, audit readability, and proactive timing in real use before treating the architecture claims as proof of a safe, reliable system."
      }
